# Build context for the image. Docker anchors a slash-less pattern to the
# context root (unlike .gitignore), so depth-independent patterns below carry
# a "**/" prefix.
**/.git
**/.venv
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.github/
**/tests/
**/docs/
**/recordings/
**/chat/
# Runtime secrets: config, tokens, cloud credentials, and the atomic-write temp
# files around them (config.py writes "<name>.json.tmp", youtube_streamer.py
# writes ".<name>.<random>.tmp"). The image holds none of these, because the
# Dockerfile copies a fixed list of paths rather than the whole context; these
# patterns are the second line of defence for a future `COPY . .`. The trailing
# "*" on config also covers config.json.example, which the image does not need.
**/config*.json*
**/client_secret*.json
**/credentials*.json
**/youtube_token*.json
**/update_state*.json*
**/*.json.tmp
**/.*.tmp
**/*.chat.json
**/*.chat.json.tmp
**/*.bak
# Key material: tunnel state, service-account keys, PEM files.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/.env*
# .tz: nothing in this repo reads these files. The filter covers host tooling
# that writes them next to a checkout.
**/.tz
**/cloudflared/
# ":Zone.Identifier" is the Windows download marker.
**/*:Zone.Identifier
**/build/
**/dist/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.log
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/.DS_Store
